.com/users/ijjk","html_url":"https://github.com/ijjk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijjk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijjk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijjk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijjk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijjk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijjk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijjk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijjk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ijjk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-05-15T17:43:13Z","updated_at":"2019-05-15T17:43:13Z","body":"It looks like this is due to you using two separate Next.js insallations. When you install `next` in the `e2e` folder and then import `../../lib` it imports the `next` installed to your project's `node_modules`.\r\n\r\nIt works fine if you remove `node_modules`, `next.config.js`, and `.babelrc` from `e2e` and upgrade to `next@canary` in the project then run `yarn next e2e` from the project root.\r\n\r\nI'm gonna close this issue now since it doesn't appear to be due to Next.js. If you're still having trouble feel free to reply. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/492753570/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/492792088","html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/7339#issuecomment-492792088","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/7339","id":492792088,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5Mjc5MjA4OA==","user":{"login":"garmeeh","id":13333582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMzMzNTgy","avatar_url":"ht